  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A string SSS is called Chef's favourite if every substring `chef` in SSS must have a substring `code` before it.\n\nYou are given a string SSS of size NNN that contains both `code` and `chef` as a substring. Please determine if SSS is Chef's favourite.\n\n**Note**: A substring is a continuous part of string which can be obtained by deleting some (may be none) character's from the beginning and some (may be none) character's from the end.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains an integer TTT - the number of test cases. The test cases then follow.\nThe first line of each test contains an integer NNN - the size of the string.\nThe second line of each test contains a string SSS.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a single line `AC` if SSS is Chef's favourite, or `WA` otherwise.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤1041 \\leq N \\leq 10^41≤N≤104",
      "∣S∣=N|S| = N∣S∣=N",
      "SSS consists only of lowercase English characters",
      "Both `code` and `chef` appear as a substring at least once in SSS"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n8\ncodechef\n8\nchefcode\n14\nsxycodeghychef\n21\nsxychefvsvcodehghchef",
        "output": "AC\nWA\nAC\nWA",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Substring code is present before chef.\nTest case 222: Substring code is not present before chef.\nTest case 333: Substring code is present before chef.\nTest case 444: There is no code substring present before the first occurrence of chef."
      }
    ]
  },
